5. **Rocks with Materials**: Use different materials to make your rocks look unique. You can use shaders to create effects like shimmering or glowing.

6. **Rocks with Physics**: Implement physics for your rocks to make them interact with other objects. This can be useful for creating destructible terrain or for making your rocks react to player input.

Remember to optimize your rocks to fit your game's performance needs. Use LOD (Level of Detail) to reduce performance impact when using a lot of rocks.

