DNA replication is a process where a single string of DNA is copied to create two identical strings. Here's a simple breakdown:

```csharp
public void ReplicateDNA()
{
    // Create a new string to hold the copied DNA
    string newDNA = "";

    // Loop through each character in the original DNA
    for (int i = 0; i < originalDNA.Length; i++)
    {
        // Append the character to the new string
        newDNA += originalDNA[i];
    }

    // Return the new DNA string
    return newDNA;
}
```

